  "2026-08-09T21:55:25.640Z",claude,Added scripts/docstring-gate.ts to coverageGate.sources so the launcher is held to the same 100 percent floor as the rest of the package rather than sitting outside the gate
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T21:55:25.640Z",claude,"Takes canonical adoption to 18 of 22 repositories once pm-web merges,leaving pm-csv plus pm-cli which is upstream and pm-rust which is Rust"
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-09T21:55:25.640Z",claude,"A docstring that reads plausibly from a constant list can still be false. Two similar section names were documented as aliases of one section,and reading the renderer showed they are two distinct sections the markdown path matches exactly,so the claim would have misled every caller who trusted it"
files[1]{path,scope,note}:
  index.ts,project,six declarations documented
tests[1]{command,scope,timeout_seconds}:
  npm run docstring,project,120
docs[1]{path,scope,note}:
  scripts/docstring-gate.ts,project,thin launcher over the canonical pm-ops analyzer
close_reason: Wired the canonical pm-ops analyzer in through a thin launcher and documented the six remaining declarations
body: "The six undocumented declarations were CommandError and its exitCode member, the PmItem and ContextPackOptions interfaces, and the MARKDOWN_SECTIONS and AGENT_SECTIONS constants. Documenting them required reading the two renderers rather than the constant lists: the agent renderer accepts aliases through a second include parameter while the markdown renderer matches every section name exactly."
